{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1340,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The temperature of regular stuff is basically\njust a measurement of jiggliness of the atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5830,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and molecules that make that stuff up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8120,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More jiggling, higher temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9920,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Less jiggling, lower temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12090,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, when something's at a high temperature,\nit feels hot, and when something's at a low"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15990,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "temperature, it feels cold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18330,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mmmjhyyaaanot exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19820,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you touch a piece of metal and a book that\nhave been sitting in your fridge, the metal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23350,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will feel much colder than the book - Derek\nof Veritasium did a great video on this, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27640,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you really have to try it for yourself to\nbelieve it!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29630,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The metal and the book are honestly at the\nsame temperature as measured by a thermometer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33260,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the metal FEELS colder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34980,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This isn't just a trick of the mind, though\n- we experience the metal as \"colder\" than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38730,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the book for a very physical reason: metal\nis a conductor, and paper is an insulator,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43160,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the ENERGY, or jiggliness of the molecules\nin our hands, is absorbed more quickly by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47540,
    "dDurationMs": 2019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the metal than by the book."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49559,
    "dDurationMs": 3301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though the book and the metal are at\nthe same temperature, the metal causes the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52860,
    "dDurationMs": 4289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "temperature of our hands to go down faster,\nand thus, we experience the metal as being"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57149,
    "dDurationMs": 3841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "colder - because the temperature of our hands\nis what we really feel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60990,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like how, technically, a mercury thermometer\nreally only measures its own temperature and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65290,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can only indirectly measure temperatures\nof other things by putting them in thermal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68740,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "contact with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70320,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, the thermoreceptive nerves in our\nskin can only directly measure the temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74420,
    "dDurationMs": 2829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the skin itself and not of anything else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77249,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when we touch something, we don't feel\nits temperature, but rather, we feel its effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80869,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on our skin: that is, how much and how quickly\nit transfers thermal energy - that's the jiggling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85579,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of molecules - to or from us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87929,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The capacity to transfer thermal energy is\nalso why a blast of steam from your stovetop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92409,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can feel so much hotter than a blast of hot\ndry air from your oven, even though the oven"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96259,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has a higher temperature: water vapor transfers\nmore molecular jiggling to your skin than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100719,
    "dDurationMs": 1091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "air by itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101810,
    "dDurationMs": 4689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, it's tempting to say that \"hot\" and\n\"cold\" are fundamentally different concepts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106499,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from \"high temperature\" and \"low temperature\",\neven though we usually use the words interchangeably."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110669,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Hot\" really means \"it gives off a lot of\nenergy\" while high temperature means \"it has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115119,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of energy\" - and as anyone who's tried\nfundraising knows, just because somebody has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119429,
    "dDurationMs": 12150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of something, doesn't necessarily mean\nthey give a lot "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131579,
    "dDurationMs": 17780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of it away."
    } ]
  } ]
}
